<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Welf</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Guelph, Welf dynasty, Welfs, Guelphs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Welf, or Guelph, is a European dynasty of Swabian and Bavarian origin. Its members included the dukes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-proud">Henry the Proud</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, whose rivalry with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> gave the Guelph name to a party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and Emperor Otto IV. From Henry the Lion descended the dukes of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> and kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from 1714 to 1837.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-welf.jpg" alt="House of Welf" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaiser Torikka+elements from the work of Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Brunswick-L%C3%BCneburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
